  "body": "## Summary\n\nConditional \u03ba = **0.001661948695165034** (conservative 0.00166194869228268). This is +3.14\u00d710\u207b\u2077 over PR799 (0.001661634653669567). The complex side binds; PR589's bit supplier gives 0.0017334.\n\n**Change: eight triangle-hybrid B deliveries in block 0 (new here).** On PR799's word, eight slots in block 0 (packets X = 62, 226, 228, 230, 231, 232, 236, 238) are delivered differently. In each, an entering copy E donates into a halves-copy holder so that one target read receives X+H at once. The remaining X reads swap between E and X, sw4-style, with entrance pre-reads repaired. The holders are restored by a tail at the common END frame of donor and holder (low ends) or by a FULL cleanup gate (full ends). The construction is width-neutral (3778). A frames, start/end frames and all PR799 tail frames are unchanged; 32 listed B frames are re-chosen. Each instance adds exactly +3.925\u00d710\u207b\u2078, and the eight instances are additive (the strict gain equals the ideal). Blocks 1, 2 and 13 have no legal holder for this mechanism.\n\n**Construction driver:** `construction/barch/` (standard-library builder `build_tri.py`, explicit recipe `RECIPE-U8.json`, `run_controls.py` with 38 pinned controls: identity, the recipe word, and four mutants globally and per instance: restore dropped, restore at FULL, pre-read dropped, donation after the read). All verifier code is byte-identical to PR799's reviewed set.\n\n**Independent review: SOUND.** The reviewer rebuilt the word byte-identically and ran all 38 controls at their pins, the exact replay (0 bad rows, dyadic, inverse and adjoint), audit_local, the native chain, 95 layer-end controls and its own restoration and ordering mutants. It checked the port instance X=62 specifically. Its own strict run on independently built locals reproduces this \u03ba.\n\n## Verification\n\nFrom a fresh clone of commit 73e86f69, with no reused artifacts (Windows, CPython 3.11.11):\n- `verify_manifest.py`: PASS, 138 files\n- `reproduce.py`, `reproduce_notri.py`, `reproduce_np.py`, `reproduce_p6n.py`, `reproduce_promo.py --k p6n-k4`, `reproduce_sw4.py`, `reproduce_jx.py`: PR799's word rebuilt, every layer's controls passing\n- `reproduce_barch.py --recipe U8`: U8 word rebuilt, all controls at their pins\n- `audit_local.py`: PASS_INDEPENDENT_EXACT_FORWARD_AND_DUAL_ENDPOINT_FRAMES_ENTRANCES_CONES\n- `verify_global.py`: **PASS_GAUGE44_NATIVE_EXACT_GLOBAL_ASSEMBLY 0.001661948695165034**\n\n## Scope\n\nConditional on PR645's premises and PR589's bit-supplier assumptions. No unconditional theorem or Lean certification is claimed.\n\n## Credits\n\n- **chafreaky** (PR741, PR685, PR660): the frames, the owner map and the exact-flow packing inherited from PR799.\n- **icekylinx** (PR645): gauge44 construction, package and verifier.\n- PR589 lineage (bit supplier); the PR601/604/617/622/627/635 lineage and every upstream contributor credited in PR645.\n\nPrepared with Claude Code (Anthropic).\n",
